@startuml
!include ../../../../../../plantuml/sodexo-theme.puml

title Approve and make payments — Approve validated payable
header Sat, 25 Jul 2026 · End-to-end discovery sequence
footer (c) Developed by <b>Mohit Kanwar</b>

hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 90

actor "Corporate Administrator" as Actor
participant "Corporate Administration Workspace" as Surface
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Accommodation Experience API" as Edge
participant "Payment Orchestration Service" as Service1
database "Service-owned data" as Data
queue "Kafka event platform" as Events



group 1. Return validated amount, authority checks, disputes, and payment terms.
  Actor -> Surface: Return validated amount, authority checks, disputes, and payment terms
  Surface -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/payments/payables/{payableId}
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: Return validated amount, authority checks, disputes, and payment terms.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Authorise and query
  Service1 -> Data: Read or commit Payment Orchestration Service data
  Service1 --> Edge: Scoped result
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

group 2. Record financial approval within the actor’s authority.
  Actor -> Surface: Record financial approval within the actor’s authority
  Surface -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/payments/payables/{payableId}/approval
  Gateway -> Edge: JWT, tenant scope, correlation ID
  Edge -> Service1: Record financial approval within the actor’s authority.
  alt authorised and valid
  Service1 -> Service1: Validate transition and persist
  Service1 -> Data: Read or commit Payment Orchestration Service data
  Service1 -> Events: Publish committed domain event
  Service1 --> Edge: Accepted state and next actions
  Edge --> Surface: Response envelope
  Surface --> Actor: Updated journey state
else validation, state, or dependency failure
  Service1 --> Edge: Problem details + retryability
  Edge --> Surface: Safe error and next action
  Surface --> Actor: Correct, retry later, or escalate
end
end

@enduml
